  "query_preview": "..\n\n - Meteorological Overview:\n\nStrong southwesterly flow ahead of an approaching upper-level\ntrough will bring ample moisture and forcing into the region\nallowing for scattered to widespread afternoon showers and\nthunderstorms on Thursday and Friday. A few may become severe \nwith the main concern being strong wind gusts. Additionally, \nlightning will be a concern as these thunderstorms are expected to\nbe a mix of wet and dry with the dry thunderstorms posing the \nhighest risk for new fire starts.\n\nTowards the weekend the trough starts to move eastward and turns\ninto a cutoff low which will bring cooler temperatures and a\nchance for widespread precipitation to the region through Sunday.\nBy the beginning of next week some weak transient ridging tries to\nbuild over the intermountain west but it does not last long as\nanother Pacific trough starts to make its way towards Montana by\nthe middle of next week bringing yet another chance for more\nunsettled weather. -thor",
